Backport of BED-39 (0187cb7, openmrs/openmrs-module-bedmanagement#116, merged 2026-06-15) to
the 7.2.0 tag: prevent a premature Hibernate flush in EncounterWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler.

7.2.0 predates it. There, saving a visit also runs the save handlers of its encounters, and
EncounterWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler calls saveBedPatientAssignment() for every
non-voided bed assignment on those encounters, ended ones included. saveBedPatientAssignment()
needs "Assign Beds" and "Edit Admission Locations". So even with patch 0001, a user without bed
write access could not end a visit in which the patient had a bed that has since been freed.

Pointed out in review of openmrs/openmrs-module-bedmanagement#119. On the 7.2.0 tag, with 0001
alone the module's api tests run 121 with 1 error (APIAuthenticationException from
saveBedPatientAssignment); with this patch as well, all 124 pass. Main source only, as in the
upstream commit; its unit test is not part of the build.

Applied by distribution/backend/Dockerfile (bedmanagement stage), after 0001. Tracked in
packages/modify-pr/.patches/0006-openmrs-module-bedmanagement-backport-bed-39.md.

diff --git a/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/bedmanagement/aop/EncounterWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler.java b/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/bedmanagement/aop/EncounterWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler.java
index cf34fe0..720d7b0 100644
--- a/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/bedmanagement/aop/EncounterWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler.java
+++ b/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/bedmanagement/aop/EncounterWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler.java
@@ -48,10 +48,24 @@ public class EncounterWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler implements SaveHandler
 			List<BedPatientAssignment> bpaList = bedManagementService.getBedPatientAssignmentByEncounter(encounter.getUuid(),
 			    true);
 			
+			// The bpa instances below are already persistent and attached to the current
+			// Hibernate
+			// session, so mutating them is enough: the changes are flushed with the
+			// surrounding
+			// transaction. We deliberately avoid calling the @Transactional
+			// bedManagementService
+			// save/delete methods here, because their commit forces an early flush of the
+			// whole
+			// session and can trip over unrelated, not-yet-populated entities (e.g. a
+			// VisitAttribute
+			// whose NOT NULL valueReference has not been serialized yet).
 			if (encounter.getVoided()) {
 				log.debug("Voiding beds due to voided encounter");
 				for (BedPatientAssignment bpa : bpaList) {
-					bedManagementService.deleteBedPatientAssignment(bpa, "encounter voided");
+					bpa.setVoided(true);
+					bpa.setDateVoided(date);
+					bpa.setVoidReason("encounter voided");
+					bpa.setVoidedBy(user);
 					log.debug("Voided bedPatientAssignment for bed " + bpa.getBed());
 				}
 			}
@@ -60,7 +74,6 @@ public class EncounterWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler implements SaveHandler
 			for (BedPatientAssignment bpa : bpaList) {
 				log.debug("updating bedPatientAssignment starttime for bed " + bpa.getBed());
 				bpa.setStartDatetime(encounterDatetime);
-				bedManagementService.saveBedPatientAssignment(bpa);
